This template formats daily editions of ''The Toyozawa Mainichi'' as a newspaper-style page with a side-by-side masthead, section headers, and broadsheet styling. The masthead features the portrait logo on the left with Toyozawa identity elements on the right.

==Usage==
<pre>
{{Toyozawa Mainichi edition
| date = 9 June 2026
| era = Jutsu 15
| edition_note = Morning Edition
| headlines = 
'''Headline 1'''
Story text...

| entertainment = 
'''Headline'''
Story text...

| international = 
'''Headline'''
Story text...

| sports = 
'''Headline'''
Story text...

| worldcup = 
'''Headline'''
Story text... (2026 AFA World Cup — 14 June to 15 July; omit outside tournament)

| editorial = 
'''Editorial Title'''
Editorial text...

'''Columnist Name — Column Title'''
Column text...

| toyozawa = 
'''Headline'''
Story text...

| regional = 
'''[Prefecture/City]'''
'''Headline''' — Story text.

}}
</pre>

==Parameters==
* '''date''' (required): Publication date, e.g. "9 June 2026"
* '''era''' (required): Jutsu era date, e.g. "Jutsu 15"
* '''edition_note''' (optional): Edition type, defaults to "Morning Edition"
* '''headlines''' (required): Front-page stories
* '''entertainment''' (optional): Entertainment and culture
* '''international''' (optional): International news
* '''sports''' (optional): Sports stories
* '''worldcup''' (conditional): 2026 AFA World Cup coverage — only renders if parameter is provided; use during tournament (14 June – 15 July 2026)
* '''editorial''' (required): Editorials, columns, and opinion pieces — the Mainichi's signature section
* '''toyozawa''' (required): Toyozawa city and metropolis news — the paper's home section
* '''regional''' (optional): Regional news briefs with location subheaders

==Design Notes==
The Toyozawa Mainichi uses a distinct visual identity from the Okami Times:
* '''Masthead layout:''' Side-by-side — portrait logo (160px) on the left, paper identity on the right. The right column displays the paper name, Japanese name (豊沢毎日), establishment date, and Toyozawa identity tags (The Forge · Nation's Kitchen · City of Temples).
* '''Font:''' Palatino Linotype (vs. Georgia) — a more authoritative, industrial book-face serif
* '''Section headers:''' 22px bold with letter-spacing (vs. 18px) — larger, more commanding
* '''Header style:''' Thick solid border under section names (vs. gold underline) — heavier, more serious
* '''Background:''' #ede9e0 with gradient masthead (vs. flat #faf8f2) — warmer, more industrial
* '''Borders:''' 2px solid #3a2a1a (vs. 1px) — heavier frame
* '''Editorial section:''' Light background (#f5f2ec) with gold border to visually distinguish the signature opinion section
* '''Toyozawa section:''' Same light background (#f5f2ec) with gold border — the paper's home city section, placed after Editorial
* '''Regional section:''' Location subheaders in bold (e.g. '''[Noto/Ohara]''') above each brief, rather than embedded in the headline
* '''Colour palette:''' Darker earth tones (#3a2a1a, #2c1810, #8b6914) — industrial Toyozawa heritage

